<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Defs_L3_3_1_1" targetNamespace="https://teck.example/process-models/pillar-03">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collab_L3_3_1_1">
    <bpmn:participant id="Pool_L3_3_1_1" name="3.1.1 Primary Crushing" processRef="Process_L3_3_1_1"/>
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_L3_3_1_1" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>L0/L1/L2 Process. Jaw or gyratory crusher reduces ROM ore from truck-tipped fragmentation (typically P80 150–350 mm) to a product suitable for conveying and secondary crushing or direct SAG mill feed (P80 80–150 mm). The primary crusher is the first fixed measurement point in the process.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_L3_3_1_1">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_L3_3_1_1_cro" name="Control Room Operator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_L3_3_1_1_s</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gw_L3_3_1_1_g</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_L3_3_1_1_e</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_L3_3_1_1_dcs" name="DCS Auto-control">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Service_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Service_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L3_3_1_1_n1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_L3_3_1_1_s" name="Haul truck tip event; plant in Run state">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_1_1_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_1" name="3.1.1.1 Receive ROM Feed at Crusher">
      <bpmn:documentation>Haul trucks tip ROM ore into the primary crusher dump pocket. Tip event is recorded by the crusher management system or FMS when a truck dumps (GPS + crusher proximity sensor). Belt weigh feeder on the apron/pan feeder below the dump pocket measures ore feed rate continuously. This measurement point is the opening of the plant-side mass balance and the internal mine-to-mill custody transfer. [P754: mass | belt weigh feeder / apron feeder scale | continuous (1-min integration) | Principles 1, 5 | YES — internal custody transfer: Mine Operations to Processing]
ISA-95 level: 1 / 3
Actors: Control Room Operator; Automated DCS
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 1, 3; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 5 (mass measurement; custody transfer)
DDVC layer: Raw; Curated (process_measurement_point — crusher_feed_mass_rate)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_1_1_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_1_1_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Service_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_2" name="3.1.1.2 Execute Primary Crushing">
      <bpmn:documentation>Gyratory or jaw crusher (depending on site) reduces ROM ore to the target top size. DCS monitors and controls closed-side setting (CSS) to achieve the target product size. Crusher power draw (kW), throughput (t/hr from apron feeder), vibration, and hydraulic pressure are logged at 1-minute intervals to PI Historian. Tramp metal detection upstream protects crusher internals.
ISA-95 level: 0 / 2
Actors: DCS Auto-control; Control Room Operator
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 0, 2; AMIRA P754 Principle 2 (consistent, transparent system — crusher settings documented)
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series: primary_crusher_telemetry)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_1_1_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_1_1_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Service_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_3" name="3.1.1.3 Transport via Discharge Conveyor">
      <bpmn:documentation>Crushed ore discharges from the crusher onto the main discharge conveyor belt to the coarse ore stockpile (COS) or directly to the SAG mill feed bin. A belt weigher on the discharge conveyor provides a secondary mass measurement (cross-checked against apron feeder). Belt speed, loading, and mass rate are logged continuously. [P754: mass | belt weigher (conveyor) | continuous (1-min integration) | Principles 1, 2, 7 | NO — internal process measurement, not a custody transfer point]
ISA-95 level: 1 / 2
Actors: DCS Auto-control
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 1, 2; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 2, 7
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_1_1_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_1_1_4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_4" name="3.1.1.4 Manage Coarse Ore Stockpile">
      <bpmn:documentation>COS acts as a buffer between the discontinuous primary crusher (batch-fed by haul trucks) and the continuous SAG mill circuit. Stockpile level is monitored by level sensor or periodic survey. Reclaim feeders pull ore from the COS base onto the SAG mill feed conveyor at a controlled rate. COS inventory (mass) is estimated from level sensor volume plus density assumption; this is a known P754 measurement accuracy limitation. [P754: mass (inventory estimate) | level sensor + density assumption | continuous level / periodic survey | Principles 1, 7, 8 | NO — internal process buffer; not a custody transfer point]
ISA-95 level: 2 / 3
Actors: Control Room Operator; DCS
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 2, 3; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 7, 8
DDVC layer: Raw; Curated (process_inventory_node)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_1_1_4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_1_1_5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gw_L3_3_1_1_g" name="COS level below minimum?" default="Flow_L3_3_1_1_7">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_1_1_5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_1_1_6</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_1_1_7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_L3_3_1_1_n1" name="Throttle SAG mill feed rate and alert control room">
      <bpmn:documentation>Derived from the Process Flow Narratives section (not a row in the Process Decomposition). DCS auto-throttle when COS level is below minimum.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_1_1_6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_1_1_8</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_L3_3_1_1_e" name="Crushed ore at COS or SAG feed bin">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_1_1_7</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_1_1_8</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_1_1_1" sourceRef="Start_L3_3_1_1_s" targetRef="Task_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_1"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_1_1_2" sourceRef="Task_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_1" targetRef="Service_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_2"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_1_1_3" sourceRef="Service_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_2" targetRef="Service_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_3"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_1_1_4" sourceRef="Service_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_3" targetRef="Task_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_4"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_1_1_5" sourceRef="Task_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_4" targetRef="Gw_L3_3_1_1_g"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_1_1_6" name="Yes" sourceRef="Gw_L3_3_1_1_g" targetRef="Task_L3_3_1_1_n1"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_1_1_7" name="No" sourceRef="Gw_L3_3_1_1_g" targetRef="End_L3_3_1_1_e"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_1_1_8" sourceRef="Task_L3_3_1_1_n1" targetRef="End_L3_3_1_1_e"/>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_L3_3_1_1">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_L3_3_1_1" bpmnElement="Collab_L3_3_1_1">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Pool_L3_3_1_1_di" bpmnElement="Pool_L3_3_1_1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="20" y="20" width="1434" height="340"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_L3_3_1_1_cro_di" bpmnElement="Lane_L3_3_1_1_cro" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="60" y="20" width="1394" height="170"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_L3_3_1_1_dcs_di" bpmnElement="Lane_L3_3_1_1_dcs" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="60" y="190" width="1394" height="170"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Start_L3_3_1_1_s_di" bpmnElement="Start_L3_3_1_1_s"><dc:Bounds x="110" y="77" width="56" height="56"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="88" y="139" width="100" height="56"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_1_di" bpmnElement="Task_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_1"><dc:Bounds x="202" y="65" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Service_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_2_di" bpmnElement="Service_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_2"><dc:Bounds x="408" y="235" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Service_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_3_di" bpmnElement="Service_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_3"><dc:Bounds x="614" y="235" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_4_di" bpmnElement="Task_L3_3_1_1_3_1_1_4"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="65" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gw_L3_3_1_1_g_di" bpmnElement="Gw_L3_3_1_1_g" isMarkerVisible="true"><dc:Bounds x="1026" y="70" width="70" height="70"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1011" y="22" width="100" height="42"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L3_3_1_1_n1_di" bpmnElement="Task_L3_3_1_1_n1"><dc:Bounds x="1132" y="235" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="End_L3_3_1_1_e_di" bpmnElement="End_L3_3_1_1_e"><dc:Bounds x="1338" y="77" width="56" height="56"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1316" y="29" width="100" height="42"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_1_1_1_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_1_1_1"><di:waypoint x="166" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="202" y="105"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_1_1_2_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_1_1_2"><di:waypoint x="372" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="390" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="390" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="408" y="275"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_1_1_3_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_1_1_3"><di:waypoint x="578" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="614" y="275"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_1_1_4_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_1_1_4"><di:waypoint x="784" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="802" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="802" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="820" y="105"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_1_1_5_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_1_1_5"><di:waypoint x="990" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="1026" y="105"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_1_1_6_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_1_1_6"><di:waypoint x="1061" y="140"/><di:waypoint x="1061" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="1132" y="275"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1067" y="144" width="27" height="14"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_1_1_7_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_1_1_7"><di:waypoint x="1096" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="1338" y="105"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1100" y="85" width="21" height="14"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_1_1_8_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_1_1_8"><di:waypoint x="1302" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="1366" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="1366" y="133"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
